      "text": "Reddit threads show recurring problems when homeowners attempt do-it-yourself exclusions under houses. One user built a one-way exclusion door and reported it never triggered, indicating either multiple access points or an animal that had stopped using that opening. Another user described sealing an entrance only to find trapped young inside, which led to carcass odor and larger cleanup bills. For these reasons, professional sequencing is important: inspect, confirm the absence of young, install one-way devices if appropriate, then seal permanently.",
